                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ac6a0b8c-201c-482a-9cb1-6e18efba37a0",
                        "entry_id": "4864fb04-c81a-3d09-8f73-51b083ae5af9",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Kylies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5b8460c4-587f-35f9-b566-5ff4b8fb1f97",
                        "entry_id": "4864fb04-c81a-3d09-8f73-51b083ae5af9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A female given name originating as a coinage."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f374a3ea-ca92-48b7-9e2a-864b0409f7f5",
                                "sense_id": "5b8460c4-587f-35f9-b566-5ff4b8fb1f97",
                                "text": "Kylie and her parents had been driving through the outback for hours. They had taken a five-hour flight from Sydney, where they lived, to Perth, in Western Australia. From Perth, they had to drive another seven hours to get to Kylie′s aunt and uncle′s sheep station."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c80adb7c-2dcb-4a74-bfb6-618a0da01961",
                                "sense_id": "5b8460c4-587f-35f9-b566-5ff4b8fb1f97",
                                "text": "Emily. Em-il-y, three syllables, like a knock on the door of destiny. Such an odd, old-fashioned name, compared to those Kylies and Traceys and Jades — names that reeked of Impulse and grease and stood out in gaudy neon colours —"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ca42d3c-780c-4413-84cd-27ac7becb915",
                                "sense_id": "5b8460c4-587f-35f9-b566-5ff4b8fb1f97",
                                "text": "Finnley is the fourth daughter of Jason and Kylie Kelce, having already welcomed Wyatt, Elliotte and Bennett to the family."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "d4e23faf-e8d2-3cba-9340-fbbc49092c49",
                "word": "kylie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3b26305e-a938-440c-8df9-e287a3cd216d",
                        "entry_id": "d4e23faf-e8d2-3cba-9340-fbbc49092c49",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "kylies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "efa088c8-3d84-307e-a962-c9721db2910c",
                        "entry_id": "d4e23faf-e8d2-3cba-9340-fbbc49092c49",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A boomerang."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia",
                            "Western"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dfe3e34c-3b71-48d7-b978-8beef6e3c4bf",
                                "sense_id": "efa088c8-3d84-307e-a962-c9721db2910c",
                                "text": "Then we drove up to the cricket-ground to see them throw their boomerangs or kylies, which they did very cleverly. One of the kylies was broken against a tree, but most of the others flew with unerring precision."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e7a0a432-d9e6-455d-9244-88fe93e4ea5d",
                                "sense_id": "efa088c8-3d84-307e-a962-c9721db2910c",
                                "text": "The islanders have discovered that kylies made out of thin iron, such as ship′s tanks, are the most serviceable, and they show great dexterity in making them (see Fig. 6)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8297b77c-8538-4825-bcd4-37f18ee71b6b",
                                "sense_id": "efa088c8-3d84-307e-a962-c9721db2910c",
                                "text": "Kylies were used by prehistoric people in all parts of the world. Usually made of wood, they were banana shaped; both faces of each arm were carved into curved, airfoil surfaces."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
